WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.690
As our calendars approach 2020, the reigning
king of the streaming wars, Netflix, is getting

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.260
rid of a number of movies to make room for
everything that's coming to the site at the

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.160
start of the new year.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.920
These are the movies you have to watch before
they leave Netflix in January 2020.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.760
Even in a brand-new decade, Grease is still
the word - but it won't retain that status

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.560
on Netflix after January 31, 2020.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.530
The 1978 film, a silver-screen adaptation
of the 1971 musical of the same name, features

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:33.090
Olivia Newton-John and John Travolta as a
pair of clique-crossed high school sweethearts

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.750
who navigate their whirlwind romance, the
status quo at Rydell High, and greaser culture

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.580
with plenty of song and dance.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.720
If you've somehow yet to see Grease and are
unfamiliar with the rockin'-and-rollin' Danny

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.320
Zuko and his sweet-turned-sassy Australian
squeeze Sandy Olsson, now's the perfect time

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.380
to catch the film from the comfort of your
couch.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.960
And if you're like the vast majority of people
in the world and simply can't resist the charms

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.149
of the film's characters and infectiously
cheery soundtrack, don't miss out on streaming

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:02.130
Grease for the thousandth time on Netflix
before the month is up.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.600
Taking a hard left turn away from the feel-good
fun of Grease, we arrive at American Psycho

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.960
- director Mary Harron's half-black-comedy,
half-psychological-horror that adapts Bret

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:16.429
Easton Ellis' novel of the same name into
a story that simmers below the surface before

00:01:16.429 --> 00:01:18.300
it splatters all over the place.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:23.380
Released in April 2000 to much critical acclaim,
American Psycho centers around the well-to-do,

00:01:23.399 --> 00:01:28.609
detail-oriented investment banker Patrick
Bateman, whose obsessions, insecurities, and

00:01:28.609 --> 00:01:31.040
penchant for extreme violence build to bursting.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.260
"I guess…

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:35.800
I'm a pretty…

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.220
I mean, I guess I'm a pretty sick guy."

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:46.120
This one's not for the faint of heart or anyone
with a fear of chainsaws, but for those wanting

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:51.350
a terrifying flick to get sucked into, you
have until January 31, 2020 to watch American

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.460
Psycho on Netflix.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.340
Before she was a teen girl who fell in love
with a vampire, prior to her string of acclaimed

00:01:57.349 --> 00:02:01.560
indie flicks, and years ahead of her stint
as one of Charlie's Angels, Kristen Stewart

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.740
splashed onto the Hollywood scene with her
breakout film role in 2002's Panic Room.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:10.810
In director David Fincher's thriller, Stewart
stars as Sarah Altman, the daughter of Jodie

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.420
Foster's character Meg Altman.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.860
The mother-daughter pair move into a new home
- a multi-story brownstone nestled in New

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.820
York City's Upper West Side neighborhood - following
Meg's recent divorce.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.280
You may predict where the plot is headed - that
Meg and Sarah's new home is haunted by entities

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.600
hungry for revenge - but Panic Room plays
out differently.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:33.060
Meg and Sarah discover that the previous owner
of the home built a "panic room," a fortified

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.569
hiding place to protect occupants in the event
of a home invasion, natural disaster, or other

00:02:37.569 --> 00:02:38.740
threat of the same ilk.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.880
But that's not all that's inside the home.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.480
Trouble comes knocking on the Altmans' door
the very first night they move in: the grandson

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.549
of the previous owner, Junior - along with
his two accomplices Burnham and Raoul - break

00:02:49.549 --> 00:02:53.760
into the home in search of $3 million locked
in a floor safe inside the panic room.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.160
The Altmans engage in a life-or-death game
of cat-and-mouse with the trio of home invaders,

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.520
who are determined to seize the money by whatever
means necessary.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:06.020
Panic Room is available to stream on Netflix
until January 31, 2020.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:12.100
2019 saw the theatrical launch of Zombieland:
Double Tap, the long-awaited sequel to 2009's

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.680
beloved zombie comedy Zombieland.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.240
The flick, directed by returning helmer Ruben
Fleischer, catapulted the property back into

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.930
pop culture consciousness, and had people
scrambling to rewatch the original Zombieland.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.160
"Heh heh heh heh heh heh!"

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.920
Whether you saw the sequel in cinemas or decided
to skip it, the OG flick holds up better than

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:36.249
Twinkies do in a zombie apocalypse - so in
January 2020, sit down with "mad person disease"

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:40.749
survivors Tallahassee, Columbus, Wichita,
and Little Rock and watch as they fight off

00:03:40.749 --> 00:03:45.569
hordes of zombies, share their rules for avoiding
death, and form their dysfunctional-yet-lovable

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:46.620
makeshift family.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.500
Zombieland leaves Netflix on January 31, 2020.

